%% M6 socket authorisation: JWT in the handshake, then a room check on every join.
%% Refresh tokens never leave the server; the browser gets a short-lived access token from the BFF.
%% Rooms: tracking:<no> public, user:<sub> owner, dispatch staff (contracts/openapi/tracking-service.v1.yaml).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor CU as Customer browser
    participant BFF as Next.js BFF<br/>/api/bff/socket-token
    participant KC as Keycloak<br/>realm swiftdrop
    participant SG as Socket.IO gateway<br/>/ws/tracking
    participant JW as JwtVerifier<br/>shared lib
    participant RP as RoomPolicy

    CU->>BFF: GET /api/bff/socket-token (encrypted session cookie)
    BFF->>BFF: read access token from session, no refresh token
    BFF-->>CU: short-lived access token (aud swiftdrop-api)
    CU->>SG: connect, handshake auth.token
    SG->>JW: verify(token)
    JW->>KC: fetch JWKS (cached)
    KC-->>JW: public keys
    alt signature, issuer, audience or expiry fails
        JW-->>SG: invalid
        SG-->>CU: connect_error unauthorized, disconnect
    else valid
        JW-->>SG: Principal {sub, roles, merchantId}
        SG-->>CU: connected

        CU->>SG: join user:OWN_SUB
        SG->>RP: canJoin(principal, user:OWN_SUB)
        RP-->>SG: allow
        SG-->>CU: joined

        CU->>SG: join user:OTHER_SUB
        SG->>RP: canJoin(principal, user:OTHER_SUB)
        RP-->>SG: deny (sub differs)
        SG-->>CU: error forbidden, room not joined

        CU->>SG: join dispatch
        SG->>RP: canJoin(principal, dispatch)
        RP-->>SG: deny (role CUSTOMER)
        SG-->>CU: error forbidden, room not joined
    end

    Note over CU,SG: Anonymous socket with no token can only join public tracking rooms, user rooms and dispatch are refused.
